1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,647
Illiquidity means you may not be
able to turn an investment into

2
00:00:03,647 --> 00:00:05,232
cash when you want.

3
00:00:05,232 --> 00:00:08,956
Private startup securities usually
do not trade on an exchange with

4
00:00:08,956 --> 00:00:11,224
a continuous list of buyers.

5
00:00:11,224 --> 00:00:15,619
In Reg CF, resale is generally
restricted for the first year,

6
00:00:15,619 --> 00:00:17,964
subject to limited exceptions.

7
00:00:17,964 --> 00:00:21,714
After that period, there is still no
guarantee that anyone will buy

8
00:00:21,714 --> 00:00:25,606
your security, or that a transfer is
allowed under the company’s

9
00:00:25,606 --> 00:00:26,830
documents.

10
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:31,121
A company may take years to
have a sale, public listing, or other

11
00:00:31,121 --> 00:00:33,686
event that creates a possible
payout.

12
00:00:33,686 --> 00:00:35,335
It may never happen.

13
00:00:35,335 --> 00:00:39,626
For example, investing $1,000
does not mean you can request

14
00:00:39,626 --> 00:00:42,358
the $1,000 back next month.

15
00:00:42,358 --> 00:00:45,490
Plan as though the money could
be tied up indefinitely and could

16
00:00:45,490 --> 00:00:47,307
ultimately be lost.

17
00:00:47,307 --> 00:00:51,263
Before investing, check transfer
restrictions, any company

18
00:00:51,263 --> 00:00:55,206
approval requirements, and what
events could create liquidity.

19
00:00:55,206 --> 00:00:58,918
A reported valuation or a new
funding round is not the same as

20
00:00:58,918 --> 00:01:00,576
cash you can withdraw.

